Friday Night Funkin' — classic Week 1 browser recreation

Original game by ninjamuffin99 (programming), PhantomArcade and evilsk8r
(art and animation), and Kawai Sprite (music).

This fan-made browser implementation is independent of The Funkin' Crew.
It is not an official release and does not imply their endorsement.

Original visual assets, fonts, audio and charts were obtained from the
FunkinCrew/Funkin repository at tag v0.2.7.1:
https://github.com/FunkinCrew/Funkin/tree/v0.2.7.1

The original tag's Apache 2.0 LICENSE is included in this distribution.
The assets are from that historical tag, not the current funkin.assets tree.
Assets retain their original names and artwork. Sparrow XML sprite indexes
are also converted into assets/atlases.json; invalid nameless entries are omitted.

The JavaScript Canvas/Web Audio engine, controls, settings, accessibility
hit targets, result screen, and GitHub Pages packaging are a new implementation.
This is a recreation of the classic Week 1 experience, not a verbatim Haxe port.

Friday Night Funkin' and its logo belong to their respective owners.
Support the original game: https://ninja-muffin24.itch.io/funkin

Modern menu artwork, character animation, Erect/Pico arrangements and charts
were extracted from the user's installed Friday Night Funkin archive.
These modern assets retain their respective creators' copyrights; the
historical Apache license above describes the classic tagged distribution.
See assets/modern/provenance.json and assets/variants/catalog.json for the
specific source entries, musical credits and chart credits.

Classic sprite sheets were mechanically repacked, duplicate texture pixels
removed, and physical texture resolution reduced while preserving logical
frame geometry. Adobe Animate timelines were flattened into compact atlases.
Modern charts were converted into the classic format without changing note
times, ownership or sustain lengths. Split vocal stems were synchronized
and merged for playback in this engine.

Week 2 songs, Spooky Month stage artwork, character-select spotlight movie,
music and animation timelines are also extracted from the same installed game.
The ZIP mod reader and compatibility layer are an independent browser
implementation; imported archives stay in browser storage and are not uploaded.

Tutorial, Weeks 3/4, native result screens, full character special/reaction
symbol trees, Pico gun backing-card layers and Erect stage props were
extracted from the user's installed V-Slice 0.8.6 assets. Original authors'
copyrights remain intact. Native metadata, arrangement/chart credits and
source paths are retained in assets/native-content.json,
assets/native-extras/*.json, assets/native-results/*.json and the variant
catalog. The historical LICENSE is not a claim that all modern artwork is
licensed under that historical license. The six-key arrangement is generated
by this browser recreation and is not an original Funkin Crew chart.
